From e8347c3d5ab457043356f64deeeb63d660cea104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:03:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 099/107] video: rockchip: mpp: do not report a stale IRQ
 status for a timed-out task

mpp->irq_status is written only by the codec hard-IRQ callbacks and is
never cleared. When a task times out, the default worker still calls the
backend ISR, which copies mpp->irq_status into the task. For AV1, RKVENC2,
IEP2 and non-link RKVDEC2 the timed-out task therefore inherits the last
latched status, normally the previous frame's success, and userspace is
told the hung frame completed cleanly.

Clear the latched status in the timeout branch, while the codec IRQ is
still disabled, so the backend reports no completion bits.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
index 66c590e900a7..5e3400a40f50 100644
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
@@ -1078,6 +1078,14 @@ static void try_process_running_task(struct mpp_dev *mpp)
 		if (test_bit(TASK_STATE_TIMEOUT, &mpp_task->state)) {
 			atomic_inc(&mpp->reset_request);
 			mpp_iommu_dev_deactivate(mpp->iommu_info, mpp);
+			/*
+			 * No completion IRQ arrived for this task.  irq_status
+			 * still holds whatever the last hard IRQ on this core
+			 * latched, usually the previous frame's success, and
+			 * the backend ISR below would report that as this
+			 * task's result.
+			 */
+			mpp->irq_status = 0;
 		}
 
 		if (mpp->auto_freq_en && mpp->hw_ops->reduce_freq &&
